From 9fb550c41d594960aff35a8d3c7bc6ae532e3a1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iav <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:06:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/49] rocket/rk3568: fix depthwise, pad value and
 KERNEL_GROUP

Three more differences read off the vendor command stream:

- rkt_task.c doubled output_channels for depthwise layers with 32 or fewer
  channels and aligned the result to 64.  RK3568 wants the real count: the
  vendor writes DPU_DATA_CUBE_CHANNEL 0x001f001f for every 32-channel
  depthwise layer of mobilenet_v1, where mesa announced 64 channels to the
  DPU, which then waited for data that never arrived and stalled right after
  CNA.  Depthwise layers now complete.
- The pad value lives in the upper half of CNA_PAD_CON0, not in the separate
  PAD_CON1 register registers.xml lists -- the vendor never writes 0x1184 at
  all.  Mesa already computed the right number (input_zero_point - 0x80) and
  put it in the wrong place, so every padded convolution padded with zero
  instead of with the zero point.
- CNA_CONV_CON2 KERNEL_GROUP stays zero in all 51 vendor tasks, including
  layers with 512 and 1001 kernels; mesa's kernels/32 - 1 underflowed to 0xff
  on depthwise.
- CNA_CBUF_CON1 DATA_ENTRIES is twice what mesa computed.

Single-layer tests at mobilenet_v1 shapes -- depthwise 3x3 stride 1 and
stride 2 at 112x112x32, plain 3x3 at 56x56x32, and the 80x80x16 to
40x40x128 reference -- now all run without a timeout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
