Subject: [PATCH 08/49] rocket: RK3568 vendor per-channel requant + atomic
 broadcast unit start

The DPU BS stage now takes all three per-channel operands from the BRDMA
stream (8 bytes per channel, packed [bias i32 x4][ow i16 x4][mul u16 x4]),
matching the vendor stack: BS_CFG 0x148, BS_MUL_CFG 0xe01 (shift 14),
DATA_FORMAT 0xe0, OW_SRC in BS_OW_CFG, BRDMA_DATA_USE 7.  The ow operand
is 0x80 - weight_zero_point: the hardware adds ow * sum(x) to the
accumulator.  The layer-level scale stays in OUT_CVT as before.

The five processing units must be started atomically with the broadcast
write (target 0x81, reg 8, value 0x1f) like the vendor stream does on
every task; starting them one at a time desynchronizes the pipeline and
scrambles the BRDMA operand lanes (verified by replaying a captured
vendor task through this driver: sequential OP_EN corrupts 41% of the
output bytes, the broadcast start is byte-exact).

layer-identity now matches the CPU reference exactly on all fills,
reproducibly across processes.  Env-gated RE probes (RKT_PROBE, RKT_WPOKE,
RKT_WLAY, RKT_BSCFG, RKT_DF0) are left in for the ongoing weight-layout
investigation of regular NxN convolutions.
