From dd57f25faeba395cb27368d58daf6e7ae0563c9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 21:05:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/49] rocket: RK3568 ARGB first-layer path (Cin=3)

Vendor-verified against a live probe-RGB capture and the mobilenet_v1
task stream:

- CONV_CON1 ARGB_IN=10, RGB_BYTELENGTH = W * H_band * 9;
- input: packed RGB rows (3 bytes per pixel) aligned to 8 bytes, raw
  uint8 -- the CNA CVT stage shifts into the signed domain with
  scale 16384 / offset -128 / truncate 14 (alpha lane scale 1);
- weight layout: same 16-kernel tap-major grouping with an 8-byte
  kernel row (ic then zero padding, byte-exact vs probe-RGB);
- band offsets in packed-RGB bytes; DATA_ENTRIES = align(ceil(W*8/32),2).

Also adds TEFLON_MAX_OPS=<K> (delegate only the first K plan nodes) for
layer-by-layer bisection of chained networks.

layer-first-rgb (224x224x3 -> 112, stride 2) now matches TFLite CPU
within 1 LSB on all probe patterns.  mobilenet_v1 still diverges from
op 3 on: depthwise with 64 channels -- the vendor emits those as
32-channel tasks; channel splitting is the next step.
