From 4d7fe9147daeba35cb8c6b0cfbf5455fb26f6990 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:43:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/49] rocket: RK3568 FC-shaped convolution path (opt-in via
 RKT_BIG_FC)

A 1x1-spatial-input convolution with a large kernel count (the final
1024->1001 of mobilenet_v1) runs as a single task with weight streaming,
matching the vendor stream (mobilenet_v1 t50):

- DPU FEATURE_MODE_CFG gains NONALIGN and SURF_LEN = align(K,16)/8
  (126 surfaces of 8 bytes for 1001 kernels) -- without these the DPU
  never completes and the job times out;
- the CNA DMA reads the 1x1xC input as (C/8) x 1 x 8;
- FEATURE_GRAINS = 1, DST_SURF_STRIDE floored at 8 bytes;
- output channels align to 16 (vendor: 1007-family values), the kernel
  count stays exact (1001, no align-to-2);
- the weight buffer stores the LAST kernel group compactly: K%16 rows
  with no padding to 16 (probe-FCL byte-exact: 62 full groups + a 9-row
  tail = 1025024 bytes).

The vendor stream carries a second DPU sub-configuration (FLYING_MODE,
OUT_PRECISION=2) that reformats the result to fp16 for its runtime; the
u8 path is self-contained and is all the TFLite delegate needs.

Isolated final layer: max 1 LSB vs the TFLite CPU reference.  Full
mobilenet_v1 with the FC delegated reached 19 ms on clean runs with the
exact CPU top-5, but the configuration-race flakes hit more often with
the extra partition, so the path stays opt-in (RKT_BIG_FC=1) until the
race is fixed; by default such layers still fall back to the CPU.
