From de50351526af5696f5e78dd5fe9405a2d3edea23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:54:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/49] rocket: RK3568 PC-chained job submission; FC path on by
 default

Let the PC unit drive a whole multi-task job through the chain tails
already present in the regcmd streams ([BASE next][AMOUNTS next]
[pre-op-en word][broadcast OP_EN 0x1f]) instead of the CPU stepping
tasks one at a time from the IRQ handler:

- fix the chain-tail AMOUNTS patcher for RK3568: the value is the next
  stream word count minus one (pc_data_amount_scale is 1; the /2 was
  RK3588);
- align the per-task streams to 128 bytes;
- emit CBUF_CON0 in the vendor head slot (between the CORE and DPU
  S_POINTER wakes);
- build a vendor-layout 40-byte task descriptor array in a BO and pass
  its address in the new drm_rocket_job::task_desc_addr field -- the
  RK3568 hardware never fetches it (the vendor runtime submits with
  task_base_addr = 0), so it doubles as the chained-mode flag and keeps
  the door open for descriptor-driven SoCs; RKT_NO_DESC falls back to
  the legacy stepping;
- RKT_STRICT emits the exact vendor word set (drops CVT_CON5, the
  WDMA_SIZE pair and EW_SURF_NOTCH, adds the 0x1210..0x1230 zeros).

FC-shaped convolutions are now delegated by default (RKT_NO_FC opts
out): with the whole chain in hardware the configuration races that
made the FC partition flaky are gone.

mobilenet_v1, 5/5 runs: identical logits (mean abs diff 0.11 vs the
TFLite CPU reference), top-5 matches the CPU order exactly, zero job
timeouts.  The layer probe suite stays at max 1 LSB.
