Average pooling lowers to a depthwise convolution with constant
weights: every tap is q=255 with scale 1/(fw*fh*255) and zero point 0,
so each contributes exactly 1/(fw*fh) and the regular requantization
pipeline does the rest.  The packed weight bytes come out as 0x7f --
byte-identical to the vendor stream (mobilenet_v1 t49 is a 7x7/s7
depthwise with an all-0x7f weight buffer).  Zero padding only: with
padding TFLite divides by the number of valid elements at the edges,
which a fixed-weight convolution cannot reproduce.

DST_SURF_STRIDE turns out to be a plain byte register (Wout*Hout*8).
The generated 4-bit-shifted helper happened to produce the same number
for even Wout*Hout (WH/2 << 4 == WH*8), but a 1x1 output needs a raw 8,
which the shifted field cannot express -- the second 8-channel surface
group landed 16 bytes out and every channel past the 7th read back as
garbage.  This also removes the MAX2 floor hack from the FC path.

mobilenet_v1 with convolutions, depthwise, FC and avgpool all on the
NPU: 9 ms, top-5 identical to the CPU reference, mean absolute logit
difference 0.03 (was 0.11 with the CPU avgpool in the middle).  Only
reshape and softmax remain on the CPU.
