Fused adds with a channel count not divisible by 32 now run as
convolutions padded to align(C, 32) kernels: the group geometry in the
weight packer runs over the padded count (the memset background of
zero_point - 0x80 is exactly a zero weight), the BS stream already
carries zeroed tail biases, and the unpack still reads only the real
channels.  This fixes such adds for single-task convolutions.

Band-split fused adds remain broken regardless of padding: every EW
surface pair except the first is read without the per-band base offset
(mobilenet_v2 add9: band 2 reads surface 2 rows 0-27 instead of 28-55;
forced 3+-band splits garble everything).  Until that addressing is
understood, the teflon frontend keeps adds on the CPU when the producer
convolution's input feature map does not fit the CBUF data banks —
replicating the band-split estimate from the tensor shapes.
