From 61b74ab6080f7ffd6c7c7fb7b82d43d91f6b3a7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 21:52:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 25/49] rocket: align feature surfaces to 4 pixels; real fused
 relu; dedup job BOs

Three independent fixes from the resnet18 bring-up:

Surface alignment (the old intermittent-failure race): feature surfaces
are padded to whole 32-byte CBUF entries -- the per-surface pixel count
is align(W*H, 4).  The vendor writes 52 for every 7x7 map (CNA
DMA_CON2, DPU DST_SURF_STRIDE, SURFACE_ADD, EW_SURF_STRIDE; 1x1
FC-shaped maps keep 1).  Our unaligned 49-pixel surfaces caused the
long-standing intermittent NPU DMA bus errors on the 7x7 network tails
(PC DMA_READ/WRITE_ERROR with a clean IOMMU): resnet18 failed 4 of 10
runs before, 15 of 15 clean after.  The EW SURF_NOTCH generalizes to
surf_stride_bytes - W*H_band*8, which covers both the band case and the
new alignment tail (vendor 7x7 full-fit add: notch 24).

Fused relu the vendor way: BN_CFG 0x92 with BN_RELUX_CMP_VALUE bounding
the accumulator to what the u8 output can express.  Output saturation
alone only implements the lower relu clamp when the output zero point
is 0; on models quantizing relu outputs with a nonzero zero point the
negative accumulator survived.

Job BO lists: drop the duplicated handle when the convolution input
doubles as the second add input (add(x, conv(x))) -- a duplicate wedges
the scheduler silently and the job writes nothing.

mobilenet_v1 0.03, v2 0.82, resnet18 max 1 mean 0.32 at 44 ms (CPU
351 ms), layer suite and conv-tiny unchanged.
