From 442b73c90fee297dde24f70791f98ea8ff044da4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 13:40:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/49] rocket: support FULLY_CONNECTED as a 1x1 convolution

A fully-connected layer over a single spatial pixel is exactly a 1x1
convolution: the TFLite [out, in] weight matrix is bytewise identical
to a 1x1 OHWI conv weight tensor [out, 1, 1, in], so the lowering just
moves the dims and reuses the convolution path (including the big-FC
weight streaming for matrices larger than the CBUF).

The teflon frontend gains the fused-activation handling the fcon
struct already had a field for.

resnet18 now runs entirely on the NPU including the final 512x1000
matmul: 13 ms, logits within 2 LSB of the CPU reference (the top-5
order swap in positions 4/5 is a CPU-side tie split by the known
irreducible +-1 rounding).  Small FC and fused-relu covered by
layer-fc-small/layer-fc-relu: within 1 LSB.  Regression clean.
