From 3dde38866d6582b5a1e854343f1dc534cfbb5146 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:30:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 31/49] rocket: size CBUF banks for the declared input channels

The band splitter counted CBUF entries from the real channel count
while DATA_SIZE1 declares align(max(C, 16), 16) channels -- and the
hardware fills entries for the declared count.  An 8-channel 56x56
single-task convolution wrote 28 entries per row into a bank sized
for 14, so every input row past 1024/28 = 36.5 read back from the
start of the bank: the tail of the output was computed from the top
of the input map.  The wrap row tracked the predicted bank boundary
exactly across probes with W = 48..112 (layer-mpW series).

Real networks never hit this: convolutions on large maps have enough
channels to make the band splitter produce multi-band tasks whose
bands stay under one bank, and the 8-channel single-task shape only
appeared in synthetic layer tests (the layer-mp56 gradient diffs that
looked like a pooling bug for two days).

The packed-ARGB 3-channel line path keeps the real count: one atomic
per pixel, verified against the vendor mobilenet_v1 t0.
