Subject: [PATCH 32/49] rocket: clip the PPU input cube to the consumed rows
 and columns

The PPU derives its window count from the input cube, rounding up: fed
more rows or columns than its windows consume, it emits an extra output
row/column and shears the destination cube (VALID 3x3 s2 pooling on
56x56: 28 columns written into a 27-wide cube -- constant fills came
back wrong, so this was an addressing defect, not arithmetic).  The
vendor clips the cube to (out - 1) * stride + kernel - padding (probe
MPvalid56 carries cube 55 for the 56-row map) while the RDMA line and
surface strides keep the full-map values; do the same.

SAME-padded pools were unaffected: there the consumed extent equals the
input extent.  layer-mpC 255-LSB diffs drop to the usual 1-2 LSB
requantization noise; the full pooling and network suite is unchanged.
