From db7ec18b86685adce11466ebcf3a70753fbf0c68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:47:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 33/49] rocket: fix depthwise convolutions with fewer than 32
 channels

Two mismatches against the vendor stream, found with offline-decoded
probes (probe-DW16k1/DW24k3/DW32k1):

The DPU cube announces the full 32-wide depthwise group even when
fewer channels are real (vendor: ORIG_CHANNEL=15, CHANNEL=31, CORE
0x3014=0x1f for C=16).  With the real count announced the pipeline
produced nothing and the output stayed at the zero point -- the
layer-dw1x1 C=16 probes read back a constant.

The weight rows must be packed at the stride the registers announce
(align(max(C, 16), 16), the DATAIN_CHANNEL/WEIGHT_SIZE value): the
generic packer used the real channel count, which only coincided for
C = 8/16 (stride equal, or the tail feeding output channels nobody
reads).  C = 24 packed 24-byte rows that the hardware read at 32, so
every real channel past the first tap shifted (vendor probe-DW24k3:
WEIGHT_BYTES 288 = 9 taps x 32).  Depthwise with C <= 32 now has its
own [tap][channel] packing branch, zero-padded to the stride.

layer-dw1x1 (C=16 identity and requant, C=32) and layer-dw3x3
(C=8/16/24) all bit-exact against the CPU reference; mobilenet v1/v2
(depthwise C >= 32), resnet18, pooling, concat and the layer suite
unchanged.
