From c53a1ee10c4a37559d1f2a155cd90cce5dbeda5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:17:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/49] rocket: lower the concat identity copy as depthwise
 when channels allow

The identity copy into a concat output slice was a pointwise
convolution with a C x C identity matrix.  A 1x1 depthwise
convolution with all weights q 255 needs only C weights and C MACs
per pixel instead of C^2.

Only for C % 32 == 0, though: a depthwise convolution with fewer
channels declares align(C, 32) of them to the DPU cube and writes
the padding surfaces too, clobbering the neighbouring slice of the
concat output (layer-concat-mixed: the C=16 copy at offset 0
corrupts the C=32 slice behind it).  Other widths keep the
pointwise formulation.
