From b53692820eed3378ae5c372034d808308d8f378b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 20:38:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 37/49] rocket/teflon: support INT8 tensors and per-channel
 weight quantization

INT8 is folded into the driver's uint8 domain at the edges: teflon
shifts every zero point by +128 and XORs constant tensor data (the
weights) with 0x80 when the tensors are created, and the subgraph
invoke/read_output paths fold the runtime activation buffers the same
way.  q_u8 = q_i8 + 128 encodes the exact same affine value, so the
whole pipeline below keeps working in uint8 -- INT32 bias data lives
in the accumulator domain and needs no change.

Per-channel weight scales use the vendor two-stage requantization
(RE 2026-08-22): the full [bias i32 x4][ow i16 x4][mul u16 x4] BRDMA
stream instead of the bias-only one, with mul = round(2^14 * s_wc /
max(s_w)) renormalizing every channel to the largest scale, which the
layer-wide OUT_CVT then runs off.  Register changes against the
bias-only scheme, all matching the vendor streams (mobilenet task 4,
probe captures): BS_CFG 0x148, BS_MUL_CFG 0xe01 (multiplier from
stream, shift 14), BS_OW_CFG 0x125 conv / 0x36d dw (OW from stream),
BS_OW_OP 0, DATA_FORMAT 0xe0 (BS_MUL_SHIFT_VALUE_NEG 14), BRDMA
DATA_USE 7, and DPU_RDMA 0x5024 -- which turned out to be the BS
stream length in 8-byte words minus one (channels*4/8-1 only held for
the bias-only stream; the full stream needs channels*8/8-1, found by
diffing against the vendor mobilenet stream after the second half of
every 32-channel group came out as unwritten zero surfaces).

The supported() gate now admits per-axis weight scales for
convolutions (all zero points equal -- TFLite per-channel weights are
symmetric) and per-channel bias scales (the bias DATA is already
quantized with them); activations stay per-tensor.

layer-i8-{conv,dw,c16,c64,c32in,chain} probes: bitwise vs the TFLite
CPU reference on most patterns, <= 1 LSB everywhere.  The uint8
regression is unchanged (v1 6 ms, v2 7 ms, resnet18 12 ms).
