From ef7af777701a697dd0ce4889b1cc563dc6151b40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 21:29:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 38/49] rocket: survive an ADD whose inputs both come from
 outside the partition

A yolo-style partition can OPEN with an ADD: both inputs then have no
producer inside the partition and the fused-add lowering dereferenced
a NULL host (SIGSEGV in rkt_ml_subgraph_create on yolov8n).

Synthesize both producers as identity convolutions: input 1 is copied
into a synthetic intermediate tensor (its identity conv also carries
the EW read), input 0 into the host, which requantizes into the ADD
output domain with the second input on the EW stage as usual.  The
invoke/read paths learn to pack a partition input that only feeds a
fused-add EW stage (host output geometry, addition-operand zero
point), and such a tensor gets its BO created explicitly.

KNOWN ISSUE: the EW contribution comes out as zero on the INT8
version of this construct (the uint8 equivalent is bitwise-exact on
uniform fills), and gradients show a spatial error on both -- the
emitted register streams for the two are IDENTICAL except one LSB of
OUT_CVT_SCALE, so the remaining difference is in the data itself;
needs the replay harness.  Tracked in RE-LOG Test 71.  Debug knobs
left in: RKT_COPY_PW (force the identity copies pointwise),
RKT_EWPOKE (point the EW read at the weights BO), RKT_TRACE_IN
(trace input packing and EW addresses).
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c     | 96 ++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c | 14 +++-
 2 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c
index 0a51bfb5385..2f8c85bca78 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c
