From 4c05b9fbe5b10196fcc45585776fb545d41ae72b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 22:10:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 39/49] rocket: fix the two defects behind the standalone-ADD
 mismatch

1. A depthwise host for a fused addition reads the EW operand with the
   wrong surface walk: RDMA_FEATURE_MODE_CFG sits in the depthwise
   feature mode (0x7816) and the first two 8-channel surfaces of the
   second input come out ~1/4 range low on every non-uniform input,
   bitwise with a pointwise host.  The identity copy that hosts an ADD
   is now forced pointwise, and the fused-add lowering never picks a
   depthwise convolution as host: it prefers the other producer when
   that is a regular convolution running later in the chain, and
   otherwise inserts a pointwise identity copy of the depthwise output
   to host the add.

2. The OUT_CVT scale encoding lost the implicit leading mantissa bit
   when rounding carried into it: ((bits >> 9) & 0x7fff) + 1 turns a
   mantissa of 0x3fff into 0x4000, the "|= 1 << 14" is then a no-op,
   and the value is 2^e * 1.0 at exponent e instead of 2^e * 2.0 --
   half the intended scale.  Any conv_scale a hair under a power of
   two hits it (0.0039062488 for the int8 addonly identity host).
   Carry the round-up into the exponent, and handle the 0x8000 case
   the same way.

With both fixed the earlier double-identity workaround is gone (the
EW stage reads a job input buffer fine), the debug knobs RKT_COPY_PW,
RKT_EWPOKE, RKT_TRACE_IN are removed.  layer-{i8,u8}-add* probes:
bitwise; regression unchanged.
