From 5fd254e29ca323711a40bc4f29616e09185172dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:36:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 43/49] rocket/teflon: fuse x * sigmoid(x) (SiLU) into the
 convolution via the DPU LUT

TFLite lowers SiLU to CONV -> LOGISTIC -> MUL(conv_out, logistic_out).
Teflon recognizes the triple (silu_pattern: the logistic and the mul
are the only readers of the convolution output) and flags the LOGISTIC
and MUL operations; rocket accepts them on that basis and folds the
activation into the convolution, which writes the MUL output directly.

The hardware path is the vendor's ConvExSwish (RE-LOG Test 73): the BN
multiplier maps the accumulator into the LUT domain (x_lut = acc * mul
>> shift, field = shift on both BS paths), EW_CFG 0x302 routes through
the lookup, OUT_CVT requantizes the table output (2 * silu(x) in LUT
units; scale = s_lut / (2 * s_out)).  One LUT domain serves every
layer: x in [-8, 8) real, 1/2048 per unit, so the tables are the same
for the whole graph.

Findings that shaped the implementation (RE-LOG Test 75):
- loading the tables from the command stream, as the vendor does with
  two DPU-only tasks, is unreliable -- only the first DPU-only task of a
  chain lands its LUT_ACCESS_DATA writes, later ones are lost or land
  partially; the tables therefore travel with the job (drm_rocket_job
  lut_data/lut_count, 2 x 515 words in the hardware framing) and the
  kernel writes them through MMIO while the unit is idle;
- the first entries of the LO table misbehave: for x in [LO_START,
  LO_START + ~160) the unit returns LO[512] * (x + 8) / 256; the LO
  domain therefore starts at -512, inside the LE range, and LUT_CFG
  0x28 (HYBRID_PRIORITY clear) gives LE priority in the overlap;
- RKT_MULSH also scales the per-channel BS multiplier, which sent the
  first BN-shift measurements astray.

layer-silu{,-i8,-pt,2} probes: max 2 LSB against the TFLite CPU
reference; yolov8n_int8 delegates all 57 SiLU activations; the existing
regression is unchanged.
