From 5996173fbd72e58ac6b1bfa9ab372ab83acd69bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 17:52:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 44/49] rocket/teflon: yolo's C2f plumbing -- SLICE, QUANTIZE
 and PAD without copies

yolov8n's graph broke into dozens of partitions on three operations
that carry no arithmetic: the channel SLICE of the C2f split, the
int8 -> int8 QUANTIZE TFLite puts on every concat leg whose scale
differs, and the explicit PAD before stride-2 convolutions.

- Views (rkt_view): a channel SLICE on an 8-channel surface boundary
  is a surface offset for its consumer (src_offset / src_channels on
  the operation; the fused-add operand gets add_src_offset), a spatial
  PAD becomes padding on the consuming convolution.  Views resolve
  when the consumer is lowered and nest; a partition output that is a
  view is read from its source at the offset.
- QUANTIZE: folded into the producer's OUT_CVT when the producer is in
  the partition and the quantize is the only reader (the pre-quant
  tensor is kept requantizable on the CPU for the case where the
  partition exports it too); an identity convolution otherwise.
- teflon: builtin SLICE mapped onto STRIDED_SLICE, begin/end masks of
  STRIDED_SLICE applied; pipe_tensor.dims_count lets the driver refuse
  lower-rank tensors (yolo's [1, 84, 2100] tail arrived right-aligned
  and was read as a 1x80 map with 1600 channels).

Fixed on the way (RE-LOG Test 76):
- band splitting with a top pad lost the last output row: the rows a
  band consumes only shrink by the top pad, whether the bottom pad is
  reached depends on the stride phase;
- a SiLU convolution cannot host a fused add (its EW stage is the
  lookup table): like a depthwise host, a pointwise identity copy of
  its output hosts the add instead;
- maps wider or taller than 2047 (the 11-bit CNA/CORE size fields;
  yolo's DFL convolution over 4x2100) stay on the CPU;
- LUT framing: entry i is word i -- the vendor's leading zero word
  put every entry one bin late, ~1.3 LSB on the positive branch
  (SiLU probes now max 1 LSB, mean 0.2).

yolov8n_int8 on bus.jpg: the same five detections as the CPU
(boxes, classes, scores), raw output mean diff 3e-4; 27 ms on the NPU
against 69 ms on four A55 cores.  Probes layer-{quantcat,pad,slice,
c2f,c2f-add,bneck,first-*,big-first-*,dfl,w2100-*} and the existing
regression pass.

Known: about 2% of fresh runs of layer-c2f-add compute one pixel of
row 0 through stale input -- a consumer starting right behind a tiny
producer inside the PC chain (RKT_NO_CHAIN=1: 40/40 clean).  Under
investigation; the vendor's DPU-only "copy" tasks between operations
look like the drain barrier this needs.
