From 5969b995995dc04e20cfd06ad256837551ad5a4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 18:29:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 45/49] rocket: nearest-neighbour 2x upsample on the DPU
 (yolo's neck RESIZE)

The vendor's Resize is a DPU-only task per 8-channel surface: the DPU
RDMA reads the surface in "unpooling" mode (RDMA_SRC_DMA_CFG 0x1249:
2x2 kernel, stride 2, UNPOOLING_EN) and the DPU writes the doubled
surface (DATA_CUBE 2W x H -- the input row count, the unpooling doubles
the rows; NOTCH_ADDR 2W, SURFACE_ADD 2W*2H*8, DST_SURF_STRIDE 2W*8).
The stream is the vendor's probe-UP task word for word with the sizes
and addresses filled in; the tail starts DPU + DPU_RDMA (0x18), like
the LUT loaders and output copies of the vendor streams (RE-LOG
Test 77).

A QUANTIZE behind a pool or an upsample is an identity copy again: the
DPU copy cannot requantize, and folding it changed the yolo scores.

layer-up{,-out,-c24} probes within 1 LSB; yolov8n_int8 goes from four
partitions to two and from 27 ms to 18 ms with the same detections.
