From 7b1bb194076cb611e3eb2441a2e6d876974eeabf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:26:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] rocket/teflon: fold the graph-input and graph-output
 layout ops into packing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

yolo exports take a float NCHW image and hand back planar CHW tensors:
QUANTIZE(float->int8) + TRANSPOSE(0,2,3,1) at the input and
TRANSPOSE(0,3,1,2) + RESHAPE(rank<4) at every output ran on the CPU
between the delegate and the user buffers (~1.5 ms on the A55 for
yolov8n).  Both pairs are views now:

- teflon flags the pairs (input_pack / nchw_export on
  pipe_ml_operation); without a plan (partition_init) the flags are
  decided from the node alone, so an accepted float->int8 QUANTIZE is
  always the input pattern and a requantizing one never is;
- the input pack reads the float NCHW buffer, quantizes with the
  consumer's scale/zero point and interleaves the channels (NEON for
  the C=3 ARGB case: 16 pixels per step);
- the output unpack writes each channel as a contiguous plane.

A delegation window that cuts a partition down to views only (no
convolution) runs nothing rather than crashing.

yolov8n: 15.6 -> 14.9 ms, detections unchanged; probes ≤1 LSB.
